==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|hvernig}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈkʰvɛ(r)tnɪx/|/ˈkʰvɛ(r)tnɪj/}}

===Adverb===
{{is-adv}}

# [[how]] ("in what manner", "in what state")
#: {{uxi|is|'''Hvernig''' segir maður „X“ á íslensku?|'''How''' do you say "X" in Icelandic?}}
#: {{uxi|is|Ég veit ekki '''hvernig''' hann hefur tíma fyrir það.|I don't know '''how''' he has time for that.}}
# what [[kind]]?, what [[type]]?
#: {{syn|is|hvers lags}}
#: {{uxi|is|'''Hvernig''' bíl áttu?|'''What type''' of a car do you own?}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|is|hversu}} / {{l|is|hve||to what degree}}

==Old Norse==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|non|hvernin|hvernug}}

===Etymology===
{{root|non|ine-pro|*weǵʰ-}}

A contraction of {{m|non|hvern}} (masculine singular of what) and {{m|non|veg}} (way).

===Adverb===
{{non-adv}}

# [[how]]

